# Components

Every HALA DNA component uses the same name, anatomy, variants, and states on Web, Android, and iOS.

## Contract

- Public API uses the same concepts: `label`, `variant`, `size`, `disabled`, leading icon, trailing icon.
- Variants are `primary`, `ink`, `secondary`, `tonal`, `ghost`, and `destructive`. Sizes are `lg`, `md`, `sm`, and `xs`.
- `xs` is web only. On Android and iOS the tap target stays at least 44.
- Required states: default, pressed, disabled, loading. Web also has hover and focus. Document any state a platform cannot show.

## Styles

Style every component from `styles/foundations.css` only. Color, spacing, radius, border, shadow, type, and motion are variables from that file. Do not hardcode those values in the component.

## Anatomy

- Give each component one job. Build larger UI from existing HALA DNA components.
- Use HALA DNA icon names from `icons/api.js` (`transfers`, `search`, `cards`). The Hala icon set from HALA DNA is the only icon set, with the Lucide fallbacks listed in `hala-dna-icons.mdc`. The same name must exist on every platform.
- Example copy is sentence case.

```text
❌ BAD   Web: <Btn type="main">   Android: HalaCTA   iOS: PrimaryActionButton
✅ GOOD  Web, Android, and iOS: Button variant="primary" size="md"
```
